From 276bda3c290b145db14d02f29a128936ca0ba239 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:54:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] Add ESP32 GPIO and shared pin arbitration

Expose a BSP-owned /dev/gpio controller through the upstream dev/gpio API,
with per-pin interrupt callbacks and complete GPIO release. Keep pad
ownership shared between BSP drivers, with chip-specific GPIO register
layouts and pin validation.

Consolidates legacy kernel patches: 0003, 0006, 0014, 0017, 0035.

Co-authored-by: Peter Madsen-Mygdal <petermm@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Peter Madsen-Mygdal <petermm@gmail.com>
